2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
[Deleted by S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
[Deleted by S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“approved casino gambling” means a casino game or any other form of casino gambling approved by the Authority under section 100(1) of the Act;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“approved rules”, in relation to any approved casino gambling, means the rules which have been approved by the Authority under section 100(1) of the Act for an approved casino game or other form of approved casino gambling;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“cage” means an area within any casino premises at which cash and casino chips are deposited, and financial transactions and the paperwork necessary to support the conduct of casino gambling are carried out;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“cash” means currency notes and coins of Singapore which are legal tender in Singapore or foreign currency;
[Deleted by S 51/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
“foreign currency” means currency notes and coins of a country or territory other than Singapore which are legal tender and circulate as money in the country of issue;
“state of intoxication” means a state wherein a person’s speech, balance, co-ordination or behaviour is noticeably affected and there are reasonable grounds for believing this state to be induced by alcohol, narcotics or any intoxicating substance.

4. A casino operator must not issue, or cause or permit to be issued, any casino chips (other than complimentary casino chips) to any patron unless the casino chips are paid for to the value of the casino chips by one or more of the following methods of payment:
(a)in cash;
(b)subject to regulation 6, in casino chips issued by another casino operator;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(c)in exchange for chip purchase vouchers issued by the casino operator;
(d)by charging to the patron’s credit card, where a transaction involving a credit card is permitted under the Act or any regulations made thereunder;
(e)by direct debit from the amount standing to the credit of the patron’s deposit account or cheque cashing account with the casino operator;
(f)by an amount debited against the patron’s credit account with the casino operator, where the casino operator is permitted to issue casino chips on credit to the patron under the Act; or
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(g)by such other mode of payment as the Authority may approve.
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]

8. A casino operator may redeem its casino chips or chip purchase vouchers from a patron, in exchange for the equivalent of any one of the following to the value of the casino chips or the amount shown on the chip purchase voucher, as the case may be:
(a)cash;
(b)a cheque issued by the casino operator payable to the patron or any other person named by the patron;
(c)an amount transmitted by telegraphic or electronic funds transfer from the casino operator’s account to an account of the patron’s choice; or
(d)an amount credited, in accordance with the patron’s instructions, into the patron’s or any other patron’s deposit account, cheque cashing account or credit account, with the casino operator.
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]

19. Any casino operator which —
(a)issues, exchanges or redeems casino chips or chip purchase vouchers other than in accordance with regulations 3 to 8;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(b)allows the use of casino chips other than in accordance with regulation 9;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(c)uses or allows the use of playing cards other than in accordance with regulation 10;
(d)accepts, refuses or refunds wagers other than in accordance with regulations 11, 12 and 15(3);
(da)allows wagers to be placed on a gaming machine or using a gaming program other than in accordance with regulation 11A;
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(e)pays or recovers winnings other than in accordance with regulations 13, 14 and 15(4);
(f)declares any casino gambling void other than under any of the circumstances mentioned in regulation 15(1) or (2); or
[S 285/2019 wef 04/04/2019]
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(g)contravenes regulation 15(1), 16, 17 or 17A,
[S 285/2019 wef 04/04/2019]
[S 635/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
shall be liable to disciplinary action under section 54 of the Act.
